content:
Wait: `problem ?? operation?.error` — if both are set, prefer problem. But once an operation error exists we still want to show it; if problem was cleared on new actions. Note `act()` clears problem before running, and `submit()` clears problem. So when an operation fails after a poll, problem is null → shows operation.error. Good.

But careful: if problem is set (e.g., cancel failed) and the operation also has an error, we show problem only — acceptable (most recent failure). Actually the most recent is the problem since it came from the last action. Good.

Now replace both alert blocks with a single one placed where the operation error used to be? The problem block currently sits right under the form. Let me restructure: keep one alert block after the form.

Let me rewrite lines around 189-191 and 225-228.

Current structure:
```
    {problem && <p role="alert" className="error" data-error-code={problem.code}>
      {t(ERROR_KEYS[problem.code] ?? "orchestrationErrorUnknown")}
    </p>}

    {operation && <div className="orchestration-status">
      ...
      {operation.error && <p role="alert" className="error" data-error-code={operation.error.code}>
        {t(ERROR_KEYS[operation.error.code] ?? "orchestrationErrorUnknown")}
        {failureReasonKey ? ` ${t(failureReasonKey)}` : ""}
      </p>}
```

New:
```
    {failure && <p role="alert" className="error" data-error-code={failure.code}>
      {t(ERROR_KEYS[failure.code] ?? "orchestrationErrorUnknown")}
      {reasonKey ? ` ${t(reasonKey)}` : ""}
    </p>}
```
placed where the problem alert currently is (right below the form). That keeps the message near the form and top of the result area. But then the operation error appears above the status block — fine, it's still visible.

Hmm, but the status block is below; a failure alert above the status panel is reasonable. However when a poll returns a failed operation, the alert appears above the status. Acceptable and arguably better (error first).

Let me do that.
